/**
\defgroup engine_core Engine core
\brief Starts the engine, runs the game loop and shuts the engine down. Three functions in `namespace Engine`.

<table class="markdownTable">
<tr><td><b>Source</b></td><td>\src{include/Module.hpp} · \src{src/Module.cpp}</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Include</b></td><td>`#include <Module.hpp>` (also brings in the transform components and the renderer backend)</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Namespace</b></td><td>`Engine`</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Examples</b></td><td>Every example; \ref ex_hello is the shortest</td></tr>
</table>

## How to use

Call the three functions in this order from `main()`:

1. **Before** `Engine::InitializePlugins()`: register anything the engine needs while it starts. At this commit that is a texture asset called `CollisionTexture` (see \ref essentials_minimum).
2. `Engine::InitializePlugins()` starts SDL and the engine modules and opens the window.
3. Set up your game: register components, bind input, create entities and systems, open editor tools.
4. `Engine::Run()` runs the game loop. It returns when the window is closed (or an `SDL_EVENT_QUIT` is pushed).
5. `Engine::TeardownPlugins()` shuts the modules down.

\genexopen{modules/HelloJanus.cpp,The shape of every Janus program}
\snippet modules/HelloJanus.cpp main
\endex

\warning Returning from `main()` after `Engine::TeardownPlugins()` crashes in static destructors at this commit. End `main()` with `std::quick_exit(0)` as the examples do. See \ref known_issues_shutdown.

## What each call does

| Call | Does | Source |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Engine::InitializePlugins() | `SDL_Init(VIDEO \| AUDIO)`, then `Log::Module()`, `Filesystem::InitializeAllResources()`, `ImGuiWrapper::Module()`, `ECS::Module()`, `Renderer::Module()` (creates the window and GPU device), `CoreEditor::ModuleStartup()` | \src{src/Module.cpp,73,93} |
| Engine::Run() | Every frame: report frame time, `Input::UpdateInputs()`, stop if `Input::ShouldQuit()`, `ECS::UpdateEntities(dt)`, start the render frame, draw editor tools, render, wait to cap at 500 FPS | \src{src/Module.cpp,30,71} |
| Engine::TeardownPlugins() | `CoreEditor::ModuleTeardown()`, `Renderer::TeardownModule()`, `ECS::TeardownModule()`, `Filesystem::TeardownModule()`, `Log::TeardownModule()`, `SDL_Quit()` | \src{src/Module.cpp,95,105} |

The diagrams in \ref engine_organization show the same thing visually.

## Things to watch out for

- Four modules are not started by `InitializePlugins()`: Memory, CoreTypes and Input have nothing to start, but **GameplayFramework** registers components, so call `GameplayFramework::Module()` yourself if you use colliders or mouse hover.
- If `SDL_Init` fails, `InitializePlugins()` logs the SDL error and calls `throw;` with no active exception, which terminates the program (\src{src/Module.cpp,76,79}).
- `Run()` keeps no state you can reset: call it once.
- The frame time reported for frame *N* is the time frame *N − 1* took, including the wait. Read it with Engine::Globals::GetDeltaTime() (\ref coretypes).
*/

/**
\fn void Engine::InitializePlugins()
\ingroup engine_core
\brief Starts SDL and every engine module that needs starting, in dependency order, and opens the game window.

Call it once, at the start of `main()`, after registering any assets the renderer needs at startup. After it returns, `ECS::GetWorld()` is ready, the window is open, and every file under `Resources/` is registered.

\engex{src/Module.cpp,73,93,Engine::InitializePlugins()}
```cpp
void InitializePlugins() {
    ZoneScoped;

    if (SDL_Init(SDL_INIT_VIDEO | SDL_INIT_AUDIO) == false) {
        Log::Engine::Error(SDL_GetError());
        throw;
    }

    Log::Engine::Info("========= Janus Engine Initializing =========");

    Log::Module();
    Filesystem::InitializeAllResources();
    ImGuiWrapper::Module();
    ECS::Module();
    Renderer::Module();

    CoreEditor::ModuleStartup();


    Log::Engine::Info("Engine initialization complete!");
}
```
\endex
*/

/**
\fn void Engine::Run()
\ingroup engine_core
\brief Runs the game loop until the window is closed: input, ECS systems, editor tools, rendering.

Each frame calls `Input::UpdateInputs()`, then `ECS::UpdateEntities()` with the last frame's duration in seconds, then renders. The loop is capped at 500 frames per second. To quit from code, push an `SDL_EVENT_QUIT` event (see \ref ex_input).

Defined at \src{src/Module.cpp,30,71}. The loop body is shown in \ref engine_organization.
*/

/**
\fn void Engine::TeardownPlugins()
\ingroup engine_core
\brief Shuts the engine modules down in reverse order and calls `SDL_Quit()`.

Call it after Engine::Run() returns. Defined at \src{src/Module.cpp,95,105}. Log::TeardownModule() runs last, so modules can still log while shutting down.

\warning Returning from `main()` afterwards crashes at this commit. See \ref known_issues_shutdown.
*/
